## Retained behavior and validation

- The shared 60-second bonus cooldown, item eligibility, normal iron/component rewards, sphere contents, and existing blueprint reward code were preserved. No DBRs were modified.
- Reversing just the rewards-table replacement reproduces the original source exactly; no unrelated source changes were made.
- The bonus probabilities total 30/300 = 10%; including `nothing`, all probabilities total 300/300 = 100%.
- The packer verified the ARC header, member names, lengths, and all five payloads. The game ArchiveTool then extracted the candidate, and SHA-256 hashes of all five members matched their source files.
- Installed archive SHA-256 matches the staged candidate: `C4769A000960D64AD4894E7D76298E90522480042EF38EF9CBB6C319F0268CD4`. ArchiveTool listed all five installed members successfully.
- Grim Dawn was not running at deployment. Scripts were rebuilt and deployed; no database compilation was needed or performed. In-game behavior has not been tested.


